    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (72.41) serving as our primary engines. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Mike Burrows (xERA 4.71), with his score inflated by a 17% boost in SP skill and a 14% dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is a high-conviction start; beyond his solid base projection, his ability to exploit the slow delivery of Brandon Pfaadt (86% SB conversion probability) makes him a critical asset in our pursuit of category-scarcity points. While **Kyle Tucker** (67.05) remains an elite presence against Kyle Freeland, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** currently offer the most efficient path to maximizing our daily production.\n\nOur lineup construction remains sensitive to the volatility of pending lineups, though **Drake Baldwin** (62.62) provides a solid floor at C1, assuming he hits in the leadoff spot as projected. **Andy Pages** (62.29) remains a strong start against the left-handed Freeland, and **Curtis Mead** (62.15) sees his value elevated by the favorable matchup against Burrows. On the periphery, **Dominic Smith** (53.44) and **Heliot Ramos** (51.44) hover in the marginal tier; **Heliot Ramos** is particularly intriguing for his potential to swipe bags against a slow-working Kevin Gausman, despite facing a tougher arm. With **Gunnar Henderson** off today and key depth pieces like **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco** sidelined on the IL, our roster depth is being tested. **Nasim Nunez** (58.62) just barely misses the \"strong\" threshold but retains his spot in the lineup specifically to leverage his speed, as we are prioritizing stolen base potential across all nine slots to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
